<br class="Apple-interchange-newline"></p><p>-Continued from 31 Oct 24</p><p><b><u>Equipment description and location</u>,</b></p><p>-Heat Detector, near fire water pump No.1 P-6710</p><p><b><u>As found</u>,</b></p><p>-Heat detector activation alarm came and not clear</p><p>-Voltage drop (8.89 VDC) between terminal 1 &amp; 2 at field junction box FBN-CPP-864.</p><p><b><u>What happen</u>,</b></p><p>-Heat detector malfunction</p><p><b><u>Action</u>,</b></p><p>-Checked at field JB (FBN-CPP-864) and detected a voltage drop of approximately 8.89VDC.&nbsp;</p><p>-After disconnecting the detector terminals, voltage restored back to normal.</p><p>-Replaced the new heat detector and verified the voltage (20.66 VDC). The alarm was cleared.</p><p>-Performed the alarm test with CCR and confirmed the detector is functioning properly.</p><p>-Already ordered spare.</p><p><b><u>As left</u>,</b></p><p>-HDC-67010F is alarm cleared and back to normal.&nbsp;</p><p><b><u>Next plan</u>,</b></p><p>-To monitor the detector.</p><p><b><u>Documentation</u>,</b></p><p>-NA</p><p>-Link ()</p><p><b><u>Job progress</u>,</b></p><p>-100%</p>', '\\\\10.15.131.205\\Maint-Share\\01 E&amp;I\\Activity Photos\\2024-11-01, HDC-67010F, TS heat detector activation alarm came and not clear', '2024-11-01 10:26:00', '2024-11-08 18:09:26', 'PTTEP\\ZPQ.EI-Workshop', 'PTTEP\\ZPQ.EI-Workshop', false, 'ZTK') RETURNING id INTO new_report_id;
