<br class="Apple-interchange-newline"></p><p>-NA</p><p><b><u>What happen</u>,</b></p><p>-GDU Train 2 tripped by E-4850 low ionization current.</p><p><b><u>Action</u>,</b></p><p>-Performed test run and checked the condition.</p><p>-Found that pilot flame is ON but ionization current of E-4850 was low. (1.29 micro Amp)</p><p>-Cleaned and adjusted the pilot air adjuster and found that Ionization current of E-4850 built up to around 15 micro Amp.</p><p>-Started the burners and monitored the ionization currents for both E-4850 and E-4852.</p><p>(E-4850=20.15 micro Amp, E-4852 =19.00 micro Amp)</p><p><b><u>As left</u>,</b></p><p>-Now the unit back to normal.</p><p><b><u>Next plan</u>,</b></p><p>-NA</p><p><b><u>Documentation</u>,</b><br class="Apple-interchange-newline"></p><p>-N/A</p><p>-Link ()</p><p><b><u>Job progress</u>,</b></p><p>- 100%&nbsp;</p>', '\\\\10.15.131.205\\Maint-Share\\01 E&amp;I\\Activity Photos\\2025-04-02-SK-4800, TS GDU Train 2 cannot start', '2025-04-02 14:44:32', '2025-04-02 18:47:47', 'PTTEP\\ZPQ.EI-Workshop', 'PTTEP\\ZPQ.EI-Workshop', false, 'ZTK') RETURNING id INTO new_report_id;
